@page "/guides/announcements"
@inject IAnnouncer Announcer

<PageTitle>Announcements · Trailblazor</PageTitle>

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Headline" As="TextElement.H1">Announcements</TbText>
<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle" class="docs-lead">
    <code>IAnnouncer</code> tells screen reader users about changes they can't see, such as "Saved" or "3 results",
    through live regions that <code>TbRoot</code> and each modal dialog render. <code>AddTrailblazor()</code> registers
    it, so inject it where you need it.
</TbText>

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Title" As="TextElement.H2" class="docs-section">Try it</TbText>
<div class="docs-example">
    <TbStack Row Gap="2" Wrap>
        <TbButton OnClick="@(() => Announcer.Polite($"Trail saved at {DateTime.Now:t}"))">Announce politely</TbButton>
        <TbButton Variant="Variant.Outlined" OnClick="@(() => Announcer.Assertive("Couldn't reach the server"))">
            Announce now
        </TbButton>
        <TbButton Variant="Variant.Outlined" OnClick="Announcer.Clear">Clear</TbButton>
    </TbStack>
</div>

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Title" As="TextElement.H2" class="docs-section">Polite or now</TbText>
<TbText>
    <code>Polite</code> waits until the screen reader finishes what it is saying; use it for nearly everything.
    <code>Assertive</code> interrupts, so keep it for errors and other messages the user must hear right away. The
    same message said twice is announced twice. While a modal dialog is open, messages go to its own live regions,
    since a modal hides the rest of the page from screen readers.
</TbText>
<CodeBlock Label="Announcing" Code="@Announce" />

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Title" As="TextElement.H2" class="docs-section">Clearing</TbText>
<TbText>
    Live regions are part of the page, so a screen reader user browsing it later could find old messages. Each
    message leaves seven seconds after it is announced, which is time enough to be heard. Call <code>Clear</code> to
    remove them all at once, such as when the view they were about goes away.
</TbText>

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Title" As="TextElement.H2" class="docs-section">Testing</TbText>
<TbText>
    The live regions are in <code>TbRoot</code>, so render it alongside your component, and look for the message in the
    <code>status</code> region (polite) or the <code>alert</code> region (assertive). Register a
    <code>FakeTimeProvider</code> as the <code>TimeProvider</code> before <code>AddTrailblazor()</code> to move past
    the seven seconds without waiting.
</TbText>
<CodeBlock Label="A bUnit test" Code="@Test" />

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Title" As="TextElement.H2" class="docs-section">API</TbText>
<ApiTable Type="typeof(IAnnouncer)" />

@code {
    private const string Announce = """
        @inject IAnnouncer Announcer

        @code {
            private async Task SaveAsync()
            {
                await trails.SaveAsync(trail);
                Announcer.Polite("Trail saved");
            }
        }
        """;

    private const string Test = """
        var root = Render<TbRoot>();
        var editor = Render<TrailEditor>();

        editor.Find("button.save").Click();

        root.WaitForAssertion(() => Assert.Equal("Trail saved", root.Find("[role=status]").TextContent));
        """;
}
